  "schema_version": 1,
  "scientific_scope_status": "On positive weighted forests formed from two hidden stars, possibly joined by one edge, each action selects common real x and observes full Lx with independent Gaussian noise variance sigma^2 under the same pathwise coordinate budget B. Worst-case connectivity error <=delta forces every randomized nonadaptive design to satisfy q[pi^2+8a^2B/sigma^2]>=n(1-2delta)^2. At B=1/2, fixed small sigma/a and fixed delta, two adaptive full-vector actions suffice while nonadaptive action count is Theta(n). Fixed series resistance changes observations to L(I+rL)^-1x; a reviewed full-transcript obstruction needs B=Omega(d) for its noise law. Two routed O(1/n)-resistance channels remain conditional, with noise/switching/current/rail/settling unacquired. Perfectly floating unused terminals admit an O(1)-action ordinary baseline, while leakage and charging grow with terminal count. No hardware advantage.",
  "status_authority": "Scoped source integration from the user-provided closeout; producer and internal-review states are preserved as reported. This update does not certify correctness, novelty, physical capability or practical advantage.",
